The snapshot (project b4d606d, Mathlib 25730c7c) contains the same Ch07 contract as the workspace Contract.lean and Submission.lean. It has no proofs to reuse and no match for the four theorem names. It does provide every tool the child proofs cite:
- Euclid, MultiVector and IsUnitOrientationOf from Contract.lean;
- Gram–Schmidt orthonormality and span lemmas;
- Matrix.det_of_isUpperTriangular;
- AlternatingMap.eq_smul_basis_det, Basis.det_apply, Basis.span_apply, Basis.sum_repr;
- Orthonormal.inner_right_fintype;
- ContinuousAlternatingMap.apply (evaluation as a MultiVector);
- Real.sqrt_sq_eq_abs, Finset.abs_prod, Finset.prod_le_prod₀.
Mathlib has no Hadamard determinant inequality; it is obtained from the triangular Gram–Schmidt matrix. The DAG holds accepted checkpoints with exactly the needed frozen types:
- dpf_exists_orthonormal_frame_det_gram (steps 1–4);
- dgoj_covector_eq_det_mul_of_mem_span (step 5);
- rsdic_unitOrientation_eq_or_eq_neg (step 7).
Their candidate commits contain complete Lean proofs, and the runtime permits reuse by Lean name when the type is identical. All three child types elaborate in the contract scope. The selected parent type is proved from them, both abstractly and in situ from the accepted proofs, with axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.
